          %title
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            If a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivator"} derivator
            is regarded as a “shadow” of an
            = succeed "-category," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %em enriched derivator
            is an analogous shadow of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .query
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"}> Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
              \: What does “enriched
              = succeed "-category\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              \: I had the latter in mind. Just as a 1-category can be enriched over a monoidal 1-category, an
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-category." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            There are several different things in which one could try to enrich a derivator. It would be nice to be able to remain completely in the world of derivators by enriching a derivator over a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+derivator"} monoidal derivator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudomonoid"} pseudomonoid
            in the 2-category of derivators) contains enough information to make this feasible, so we either have to augment that notion somehow, or enrich over something else. At present, the latter is easier.
          %h3#enrichment_over_a_monoidal_category
            Enrichment over a monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .standout
            %p The following is tentative.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
            be a bicomplete closed symmetric
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monoidal (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\subset V'
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
            which is a 1-category and which is closed under the monoidal structure and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal-hom"} internal-hom
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'=\infty Gpd
              with cartesian
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V=Set
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi Gpd
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'= \infty Gpd_*
              (pointed
              = succeed "-groupoids)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi Set
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V=Set_*
          %p
            We can therefore talk about
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is bicomplete and closed, the category
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            is again closed symmetric monoidal, and hence enriched over itself.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,V')
                \-enriched prederivator
              is a
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mi CAT
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V CAT
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi V
                    %msup
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mi CAT
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\colon V Cat^{op} \to V CAT.
            %p
              (or replacing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Cat
              by some subcategory of it.)
          %p
            For instance, when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Gpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,V') = (Set, \infty Gpd)
            then this is precisely the ordinary notion of prederivator. We define this by reference to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p We now need to specify the axioms which an enriched prederivator should satisfy to be called an enriched derivator. Most of them are easy by analogy:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong (Der1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                takes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            %li
              %p
                %strong (Der2)
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                denotes the unit
                = succeed "-category," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                the family of functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(A) \to D(1)
                is jointly
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative
            %li
              %p
                %strong (Der3)
                For any
                = succeed "-functor" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\colon A\to B
                = succeed "-functor" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi u
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^*\colon D(B) \to D(A)
                has a left and a right adjoint
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_!
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_*
            %li
              %p
                %strong (Der5)
                For any object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I[x]
                denote the
                = succeed "-fattened" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(0,1)=x
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(A\times I[x]) \to D(A)^{I[x]}
                is essentially surjective and full.
          %p
            The last, and most important, axiom, involves a characterization of the appropriate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+exact+squares"} homotopy exact squares
            of
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
            enters the picture. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon A\to V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\colon A^{op}\to V
            are
            = succeed "-functors," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\otimes_A F \in V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
            and take their homotopy tensor product
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                      %mi h
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \otimes^h_A F \in V'
          %ul
            %li
              %strong (Der4)
              Given any square
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo
                                %mi u
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mi v
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi C
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mi g
                            %mtd
                              %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{ A &amp; \overset{f}{\to} &amp; B \\
                      ^u\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow ^v \\
                      C &amp; \underset{g}{\to} &amp; D}
              %p
                of
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msubsup
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi A
                        %mi h
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(-,c) \otimes^h_A B(b,-) \to D(v(b),g(c))
              %p
                is an equivalence in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mo !
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_! f^* \to g^* v_!
              %p
                (and hence also its mate
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi v
                          %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %msup
                          %mi u
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v^* g_* \to f_* u^*
          %p
            This should be compared with the characterizations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+squares"} exact squares
            for ordinary (enriched) category theory and of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+exact+squares"} homotopy exact squares
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,V')
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,V')
                \-enriched derivator
          %h3#enrichment_over_a_monoidal_homotopical_category Enrichment over a monoidal homotopical category
          %p
            Note that all we really needed of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
            was a place for a well-behaved homotopy tensor product of
            = succeed "-profunctors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            or a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+homotopical+category"} closed monoidal homotopical category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+bar+construction"} two-sided bar construction
          %p
            Moreover, since the only dependence on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
            in the definition is via the homotopy tensor product of functors, the particular choice of model we make is essentially irrelevant for the resulting notion of derivator. In other words, the true input for a notion of enriched derivator is an ordinary monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is reflectively embedded.”
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                When
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %mi V
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Set
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mi Gpd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,V') = (Set,\infty Gpd)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivator"} derivator
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+squares"} comma squares
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+exact+squares"} homotopy exact squares
                shows that this implies the enriched version of (Der4) stated above (which is a priori stronger). To make this comparison with the way Cisinski’s theorem is usually stated, one has to observe that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msubsup
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi A
                        %mi h
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(-,c) \otimes^h_A B(b,-)
                can be constructed as a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+bar+construction"} two-sided bar construction
            %li
              %p
                Conjecturally,
                = succeed "-enriched" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Set
                          %mo *
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %msub
                          %mi Gpd
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Set_*, \infty Gpd_*)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+derivators"} pointed derivators
                in the usual sense.
            %li
              %p
                Also conjecturally, any
                = succeed "-enriched" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                = succeed "-enriched" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %mi V
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,V')
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Just as an ordinary derivator encodes a well-behaved notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
            by their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cograph+of+a+profunctor"} collages
          %p
            Specifically, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mi ⇸
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\colon A&amp;#8696; B
            be a
            = succeed "-profunctor," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi u
                  %mover
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi v
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \overset{u}{\to} \bar{H} \overset{v}{\leftarrow} B
            its collage. Then homotopy
            = succeed "-weighted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi v
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v^* u_*
            = succeed "-weighted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi u
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^* v_!
          %p Note that unlike in the ordinary unenriched case, it is not possible to compute all limits by Kan extending along functors to the terminal category. This is because of the presence and importance of weighted limits.
          %h3#homotopy_kan_extensions_are_pointwise Homotopy Kan extensions are pointwise
          %p
            Part of the intuition behind the usual axiom (Der4) is that it says that the homotopy Kan extensions which make up the structure of a derivator are all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointwise+Kan+extension"} pointwise
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\colon A\to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mi u
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Lan_u X)(b)
            is calculated as a suitable colimit, which in the unenriched case can be expressed as an ordinary colimit over the comma category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u/b
            – hence why we assert that comma squares are exact.
          %p
            In the enriched situation, the (co)limit involved in the notion of “pointwise Kan extension” is irreducibly a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\colon A\to B
            be a
            = succeed "-functor," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mn 1
                  %mi ⇸
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(u,b)\colon 1 &amp;#8696; A
            denote the representable profunctor, and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            be its collage. Then the square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi u
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi H
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ A &amp; \to &amp; A \\
                  \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow^u\\
                  H &amp; \to &amp; B }
          %p
            satisfies the hypothesis of the enriched (Der4). (This is just the homotopical version of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+reduction"} Yoneda reduction
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                      %mi h
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(u,b) \otimes_A^h A \simeq B(u,b)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            and further restrict to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            and restricted to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            — but the latter is exactly the process of taking the
            = succeed "-weighted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(u,b)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mo !
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_! X
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            is computed as a weighted colimit, and hence the Kan extension is “pointwise.”
